  DID THE LESSON LAND   error early minus late on `fixed`:  +0.0721 +/- 0.0091  (8.0 SE, n=18)

  THE MAPPING CONTRAST, identity minus swapped, paired on seed
    lessons    on F1                    on F2                       n
    same axis    +0.5 +/-   0.3 ( 1.7 SE)    +2.2 +/-   0.8 ( 2.6 SE)    18
    split        -0.6 +/-   0.4 ( 1.4 SE)    -0.4 +/-   2.1 ( 0.2 SE)    18
  a taught separation is NEGATIVE. In `split` phase 1 is taught F1 and
  phase 0 is taught F2, so BOTH columns are predicted negative and the
  relevant one for each phase is the axis that phase was taught on.

  THE INSTANT IS THE BINDING CONSTRAINT. Orthogonal lessons do not reach
  two instants either: `split` is null on both formants at power to see
  1.2 and 6.4 Hz, with the same creatures, the same reward machinery and
  the same session length that give a fixed-target lesson its effect.

  SO IT IS NOT THE AXIS COLLISION. Two lessons on orthogonal axes coexist
  ACROSS TIME -- 0.84 retained against 0.22 -- and do not coexist at two
  MOMENTS of one utterance. Those are now separated, which no previous run
  could do, and the thing that fails is addressing an INSTANT: the reward
  reaches the right population and still cannot be made to mean "now".

  WHAT IS LEFT IS NOT A CREDIT QUESTION AND NOT A READOUT QUESTION. Every
  signal the creature is taught with is defined over a WINDOW -- the error
  is a trial mean, the baseline is an EMA, the eligibility is a decay. A
  mechanism that selects an instant has to be driven by something that
  CHANGES at that instant, and the only such thing here is the gesture
  itself, which the creature generates and the caregiver cannot see.
